Z||000000||fiero11||08-15-2001||12:21 AM||||I  am thinking of buying a 1988 fiero coupe 4 cyl. auto It has only 30,000 miles on it. It's black and has a sunroof. I just want to know how much you think it's worth. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||MD_Fiero||08-15-2001||01:09 AM||||well considering its an 88...just off of that im saying abour 1,500....but then again...thats only on the milage/year......hows the body..engine?...interior?...other stuff...gotta check on those to.<P>its another story if this is a 2nd engine...maybe 30,000 on the engine..but how many on the body?||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-15-2001||09:01 AM||||Only 30K miles, eh?  If it's in near-perfect condition (including the paint), has never been wrecked, and everything works,  I'd say $3000-$3500.  Others will say I'm insane, but that car will give you at least 100K miles of reliable service.<P>What else will $3500 buy you?<BR>*  A nice fastback with 100K miles<BR>*  A nice notchback V6 with 80K miles<BR>*  A friggin' 1993 Camry with 140K miles<P>And if you get sick of the Duke, the 88 would also be a great platform for a 3800 or Northstar swap.||||reg||14
Z||000003||Raydar||08-15-2001||09:33 AM||||To quote an often used phrase...<P>"It's worth whatever the seller can get for it."<P>Having said that, I'll tell you that I paid $2000 for an 88 4 cyl automatic coupe, with 114,000 miles, in 1997. His asking price was $2800.<BR>Sounds expensive, but it had been garaged for most of its life (it showed), everything worked and it was in good condition. <P>It was owned by a Pep Boys mechanic, but I bought it anyway.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
